1. Introduction

A mobile application is software that runs on smartphones. A web application can be accessed through a web browser. A Progressive Web Application (PWA) combines features of both mobile and web applications.

An online canteen food ordering system allows students to view food items, order food, make payments and receive notifications when their orders are ready.

2. Problem Analysis

In a college canteen, students usually stand in long queues to order food. During break time, the canteen becomes crowded.

The main problems are:

1. Long waiting time.
2. Difficulty in checking food availability.
3. Manual payment process.
4. Food ordering takes more time.
5. Students may miss their break time.

To solve these problems, an online canteen ordering system is proposed.

3. Comparison of Mobile, Web and PWA

Mobile Application:

- Installed on smartphones.
- Provides a good user experience.
- Requires installation.

Web Application:

- Accessed through a web browser.
- No installation is required.
- Requires an internet connection.

Progressive Web Application (PWA):

- Works like a mobile application.
- Can be accessed through a browser.
- Can be added to the home screen.
- Supports some offline features.

4. Proposed Solution

A Progressive Web Application (PWA) is the most suitable solution for the college canteen.

Students can open the application using their mobile phones without downloading it from an app store. They can view the menu, select food items, place orders and make online payments.

The canteen staff can receive orders and prepare food before students arrive.

5. Major Functionalities

1. Menu Display: Students can view available food items and prices.
2. Online Ordering: Students can select food items and place orders.
3. Online Payment: Students can pay using UPI or other online payment methods.
4. Order Notifications: Students receive notifications when their food is ready.
5. Order Tracking: Students can check their order status.

6. Development Challenges

1. Internet Connection: The application may not work properly with poor internet connectivity.
2. Payment Security: Online payments must be protected from fraud.
3. System Performance: The application should handle many students ordering at the same time.

